
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Line chart native tests
-----------------------
line_chart_widget/test_main.cpp tests the production widget against a recording
display, without hardware or networking. It covers point mapping, all four
clipping edges, gaps, uneven sample spacing, timestamps, markers, empty/single
readings, 100 samples, and invalid-input logging without partial drawing.
Y-scale tests cover signed and fractional labels, custom intervals, label
gutters, text bounds, tick counts, text-state reset, and invalid/dense scales.
Bar-chart checks cover zero baselines, proportional widths/heights, clipping,
tiny positive amounts, dry/missing dates, 3-pixel zero markers and bar gaps,
fractional-inch labels, and
invalid-input logging without partial drawing.
Floating-bar checks cover exact low/high endpoints, negative and equal ranges,
missing pairs, clipping, mismatched dates, inverted ranges, and invalid buffers
or widths without partial drawing.

From the repository root, using an installed C++11 compiler (PowerShell):

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\line_chart_widget\stubs -Isrc\widgets src\widgets\line_chart_widget.cpp test\line_chart_widget\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-line-chart-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-line-chart-tests.exe" }

Clang++ or "zig c++" can be used in place of g++. The stubs are exclusively for
this native test command; the normal PlatformIO firmware build uses the actual
Arduino and display headers.

Numeric history native tests
----------------------------
These tests use the same ArduinoJson dependency as the firmware. Build from the
repository root after the normal PlatformIO build has restored dependencies.
Use g++, clang++, or "zig c++":

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp test\numeric_history\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-tests.exe" }

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\numeric_history\stubs -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\adafruitio_manager.cpp src\adafruitio\feed_catalog.cpp src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp test\numeric_history\test_manager.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-manager-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-history-manager-tests.exe" }

The first suite covers strict UTC/fractional timestamp parsing, hourly and
custom buckets, partial windows, gaps, duplicate IDs versus repeated values,
raw extrema, circular bearings/cancellation, malformed responses, pagination
header formats, and 1,500 samples across 15 pages. The second compiles the real
manager against fake HTTP/TLS/FreeRTOS interfaces (no device or credentials)
to exercise complete-only publication, query/cursor construction, shared
request accounting, retry timing, stale-result retention, successful empty
windows, mid-page failure, cancellation during HTTP, throttling, cursor loops,
and the unchanged latest-value/alert-history response paths.
Daily-history checks cover 14 completed UTC dates, midnight boundaries, local
DST independence, the export's 141-record daily-max fixture, conflicting totals,
154 records across pages, and alignment-mode changes/validation.
Local-calendar endpoint checks cover UTC advancing before local midnight,
advancement after local midnight, and standard time after the DST transition.
Daily-temperature checks cover synchronized 14-day low/high publication,
minimum/maximum aggregation of duplicate records, negative lows, and missing
or unpaired dates.
Page-feed checks verify that `pages.p01-temp` is the only active subscription,
polls once per minute, and preserves the full JSON array in the latest-value
response.

Weather descriptor compile-time tests
-------------------------------------
weather_descriptor/test_main.cpp checks all six weather words, rule precedence,
strict threshold boundaries, and invalid pressure inputs using static_assert.
Successful compilation runs all checks; no hardware or executable is needed.
From the repository root (PowerShell), using PlatformIO's installed compiler:

& "$env:USERPROFILE\.platformio\packages\toolchain-xtensa-esp32\bin\xtensa-esp32-elf-g++.exe" -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc -c test\weather_descriptor\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-weather-descriptor-tests.o"

Wind direction statistics native tests
--------------------------------------
wind_direction_stats/test_main.cpp covers 16-point compass sectors and edges,
wrap-around through north, speed weighting, steadiness, calm/invalid samples,
cancelling winds, and the smallest covering range. From the repository root:

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc src\screens\wind_direction_stats.cpp test\wind_direction_stats\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-wind-direction-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-wind-direction-tests.exe" }

Wind direction snapshot native tests
------------------------------------
wind_direction_snapshot/test_main.cpp checks the compact feed contract,
required fields, numeric bounds, count consistency, null/empty/all-calm cases,
atomic rejection, current-value rounding, and the production renderer.
Integration checks cover exclusive pages.winddir-graphic activation, raw-history
cancellation, minute polling, unchanged-value caching, stale receipts/windows,
WiFi loss, malformed-update retention/recovery, and navigation.

python -m ziglang c++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\wind_direction_snapshot\stubs -Itest\combined_weather_feeds\stubs -Itest\numeric_history\stubs -Isrc -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\adafruitio_manager.cpp src\adafruitio\feed_catalog.cpp src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp src\screens\wind_direction_stats.cpp src\screens\wind_direction_screen.cpp test\wind_direction_snapshot\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-wind-snapshot-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-wind-snapshot-tests.exe" }

g++, clang++, or "zig c++" can replace "python -m ziglang c++". The executable
also accepts one argument and reads a producer JSON payload from stdin to
validate the Python/C++ contract directly. External test_winddir.py runs with
"python -B -m unittest -v test_winddir" from the producer directory, without
network access or credentials. It covers matching statistics, UTC bucketing,
73 partial-window buckets, gaps, cancellation, duplicate IDs, pagination,
publication/dry-run, and failure without partial writes.

Temperature page snapshot native tests
--------------------------------------
temperature_page_values/test_main.cpp tests the production JSON parser using
the firmware's ArduinoJson dependency. It covers the supplied feed payload, row
ordering, negative/zero/integer values, precision, malformed JSON, incorrect
array lengths and types, non-finite values, atomic rejection, and recovery.
From the repository root, using g++, clang++, or "zig c++":

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" test\temperature_page_values\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-temperature-page-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-temperature-page-tests.exe" }

Precipitation page snapshot native tests
----------------------------------------
precipitation_page_values/test_main.cpp tests the production JSON parser for
the 21 row-major chance/type/amount values, malformed payloads, strict value
types, non-finite numbers, atomic rejection, and recovery. Build from the
repository root after the normal PlatformIO build has restored dependencies:

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Isrc "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" test\precipitation_page_values\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-precipitation-page-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-precipitation-page-tests.exe" }

Hourly temperature snapshot native tests
----------------------------------------
temperature_hourly_history/test_main.cpp covers the supplied 112-hour snapshot,
exact 72-hour trimming and visible extrema, local calendar validation, DST
transitions, preserved producer ordering, leading nulls, negative/zero/single values,
malformed and empty snapshots, atomic rejection, and recovery. It also compiles
the production temperature-history screen against the fake manager and renderer
to check exclusive feed activation, cancellation of raw history, retained stale
data, unchanged-payload caching, and promoted Temperatures/Daily navigation.

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\temperature_hourly_history\stubs -Itest\numeric_history\stubs -Isrc -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\adafruitio_manager.cpp src\adafruitio\feed_catalog.cpp src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp src\screens\snapshot_history_page.cpp src\screens\temperature_history_screen.cpp test\temperature_hourly_history\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-temperature-hourly-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-temperature-hourly-tests.exe" }

Combined weather feed native tests
---------------------------------
combined_weather_feeds/test_main.cpp compiles all five production details
screens and all five snapshot-history screens against a recording display and
fake manager. It checks exclusive combined-feed subscriptions, minute polling,
row ordering, daylight/AM/PM boundaries, atomic rejection, exact 72-hour and
30-day windows, aligned wind speed/gust series, explicit leading nulls,
stale-result retention, and Back/Daily/Dir/History navigation.
Daily-temperature checks use the supplied 32-date min/max snapshot to verify
the newest 30 dates, exact endpoints/extrema, paired series, negative/equal
temperatures, producer-filled zeros, empty snapshots, unchanged revisions,
atomic stale retention, and recovery without raw-history requests.
Memory regression tests decode 1,000 supplied hours with no more than 8 KB of
live JSON allocations, inject JSON/staging allocation failures, and verify
retained-data recovery after a later unchanged feed poll. The manager suite
also checks active-only periodic scheduling, inactive cache eviction, in-flight
response rejection, failed String copies, and repeated large-snapshot navigation.
History feeds are producer-ordered/unique and are not sorted, deduplicated,
aggregated, or gap-filled by the display.

Barometer Trend checks cover all 25 supplied three-hour slots, exact min/max/
average preservation, local bucket dates, invalid/empty snapshots, atomic stale
retention, allocation failure/recovery, exclusive feed activation, and reciprocal
History/Trend navigation. Widget tests verify strict 0.8/1.5 hPa color boundaries
and exact average tick placement. Renderer tests cover all three series, bucket
centers, the 25-bar footer, allocation retry, and stale/revision redraw behavior.

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\combined_weather_feeds\stubs -Itest\numeric_history\stubs -Isrc -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\adafruitio_manager.cpp src\adafruitio\feed_catalog.cpp src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp src\screens\snapshot_history_page.cpp src\screens\temperatures_screen.cpp src\screens\temperature_history_screen.cpp src\screens\temperature_daily_screen.cpp src\screens\precipitation_screen.cpp src\screens\precipitation_history_screen.cpp src\screens\wind_screen.cpp src\screens\wind_history_screen.cpp src\screens\barometer_screen.cpp src\screens\barometer_history_screen.cpp src\screens\barometer_trend_screen.cpp src\screens\astronomical_screen.cpp test\combined_weather_feeds\test_main.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-combined-weather-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-combined-weather-tests.exe" }

The executable can also validate a real producer payload from stdin, with its
feed key as the sole argument. For the supplied feeds.csv export:

Import-Csv -LiteralPath "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\feeds.csv" | ForEach-Object {
    $_.'Sample Feed' | & "$env:TEMP\cyd-combined-weather-tests.exe" $_.Feed
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Invalid feed sample: $($_.Feed)" }
}

An installed Python ziglang package can run these commands as
"python -m ziglang c++" in place of g++.

The production shared renderer has a separate low-memory test. It checks safe
point-allocation failure/retry, direct supplied values, leading nulls, revision
caching, and stale-data redraw:

g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest\combined_weather_feeds\stubs -Itest\numeric_history\stubs -Isrc -Isrc\adafruitio "-I.pio\libdeps\esp32dev\ArduinoJson\src" src\adafruitio\adafruitio_manager.cpp src\adafruitio\feed_catalog.cpp src\adafruitio\numeric_history.cpp src\screens\history_chart_page.cpp test\combined_weather_feeds\test_renderer.cpp -o "$env:TEMP\cyd-memory-renderer-tests.exe"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) { & "$env:TEMP\cyd-memory-renderer-tests.exe" }
